1
00:00:33,241 --> 00:00:37,954
‪AGENT KIM REACTIVATED

2
00:00:42,333 --> 00:00:44,294
‪LAUNDRY HUB

3
00:00:53,303 --> 00:00:54,137
‪What the heck?

4
00:00:59,642 --> 00:01:02,562
‪Don't move, or else we all die!

5
00:01:23,833 --> 00:01:24,834
‪Get down!

6
00:01:39,974 --> 00:01:40,975
‪Get in the cart.

7
00:02:02,080 --> 00:02:02,956
‪Watch out!

8
00:02:41,870 --> 00:02:42,787
‪Come in.

9
00:02:47,208 --> 00:02:48,543
‪So, what happened?

10
00:02:48,626 --> 00:02:49,460
‪Well…

11
00:02:50,044 --> 00:02:51,296
‪They got away.

12
00:02:56,926 --> 00:02:58,887
‪FINALE

13
00:03:05,435 --> 00:03:06,311
‪Head to the stairs.

14
00:03:21,534 --> 00:03:22,535
‪Hold on.

15
00:03:23,161 --> 00:03:24,787
‪What are you doing here?

16
00:03:25,663 --> 00:03:28,333
‪Oh, you're here to save me.

17
00:03:29,083 --> 00:03:30,418
‪Hey, Park Gang Seong.

18
00:03:31,044 --> 00:03:34,047
‪Number 66 is on our side now.

19
00:03:34,130 --> 00:03:35,590
‪Put down your gun.

20
00:03:37,467 --> 00:03:40,011
‪I heard the person
‪who got my brother killed…

21
00:03:41,846 --> 00:03:43,014
‪was you.

22
00:03:43,640 --> 00:03:44,474
‪What…

23
00:03:45,642 --> 00:03:47,227
‪What are you talking about?

24
00:03:48,144 --> 00:03:50,897
‪I told you Park Yeong Gwang was killed

25
00:03:50,980 --> 00:03:52,482
‪by the South Korean bastards

26
00:03:52,565 --> 00:03:55,026
‪-during a mission--
‪-Didn't you say 66 killed him?

27
00:03:59,072 --> 00:04:00,823
‪No, what I meant was…

28
00:04:00,907 --> 00:04:02,116
‪Why are you so quiet?

29
00:04:03,993 --> 00:04:05,828
‪Go ahead and say it wasn't you.

30
00:04:09,082 --> 00:04:09,916
‪I…

31
00:04:12,252 --> 00:04:14,003
‪couldn't save your brother.

32
00:04:15,338 --> 00:04:16,381
‪That's it.

33
00:04:26,349 --> 00:04:27,267
‪Move.

34
00:04:28,768 --> 00:04:29,852
‪I said move!

35
00:04:30,728 --> 00:04:33,147
‪You think doing this will keep you safe?

36
00:04:33,231 --> 00:04:35,942
‪You betrayed the Party's orders as well!

37
00:04:36,651 --> 00:04:39,862
‪I'll talk to the South Korean authorities.

38
00:04:39,946 --> 00:04:41,739
‪You and I can defect together

39
00:04:41,823 --> 00:04:43,366
‪-and find a way to live--
‪-Shut up!

40
00:04:47,870 --> 00:04:49,414
‪Let me ask you one thing.

41
00:04:52,417 --> 00:04:54,794
‪Why are you protecting that enemy bastard?

42
00:04:59,549 --> 00:05:00,383
‪Sang-a.

43
00:05:01,801 --> 00:05:02,635
‪It's okay.

44
00:05:17,900 --> 00:05:19,777
‪To protect my daughter.

45
00:05:25,992 --> 00:05:27,785
‪Protecting the people I care about…

46
00:05:29,329 --> 00:05:30,997
‪is more important…

47
00:05:33,708 --> 00:05:34,751
‪than killing my enemy.

48
00:05:44,677 --> 00:05:46,095
‪You'll get another chance.

49
00:05:47,930 --> 00:05:48,973
‪Trust me and walk away.

50
00:06:06,449 --> 00:06:07,658
‪Hurry up and get in!

51
00:06:10,745 --> 00:06:13,122
‪I was told to move the truck,
‪so I had to circle around.

52
00:06:14,582 --> 00:06:15,500
‪What's going on?

53
00:06:33,434 --> 00:06:34,268
‪Mr. Kim.

54
00:06:37,939 --> 00:06:39,482
‪Let it through.

55
00:06:39,565 --> 00:06:40,858
‪SECURITY CHECK

56
00:06:44,362 --> 00:06:47,406
‪I heard gunshots, and it sounded serious.
‪Did something happen?

57
00:06:47,490 --> 00:06:49,826
‪No, it's nothing serious.
‪It's just an internal issue.

58
00:06:49,909 --> 00:06:52,411
‪-You can leave.
‪-But I have more laundry to pick up.

59
00:06:52,495 --> 00:06:54,163
‪You can do it next time.
‪Please leave for now.

60
00:06:54,247 --> 00:06:55,123
‪We have an urgent situation.

61
00:06:55,206 --> 00:06:57,166
‪-Okay, then. Good night.
‪-Good night.

62
00:07:03,798 --> 00:07:04,841
‪Close the barricades.

63
00:07:22,191 --> 00:07:23,359
‪You can get out now.

64
00:07:26,737 --> 00:07:28,197
‪-Take him to a hospital.
‪-What?

65
00:07:28,281 --> 00:07:30,366
‪But a gunshot wound
‪is hard to keep under wraps.

66
00:07:30,450 --> 00:07:32,368
‪Contact General Jang. He'll help.

67
00:07:32,452 --> 00:07:34,370
‪What happened to Mr. Sung Han-soo
‪and Mr. Park Jin-cheol?

68
00:07:34,454 --> 00:07:37,331
‪I saw them
‪getting into Ju Gang-chan's car.

69
00:07:37,957 --> 00:07:39,417
‪-Ju Gang-chan?
‪-Yeah.

70
00:07:45,256 --> 00:07:46,215
‪Han-soo.

71
00:07:46,883 --> 00:07:48,009
‪Where are you?

72
00:07:48,843 --> 00:07:49,719
‪What's wrong?

73
00:07:50,511 --> 00:07:51,721
<i>‪Kim, I'm sorry.</i>

74
00:07:55,933 --> 00:07:56,767
‪Mr. Kim.

75
00:07:57,768 --> 00:07:58,603
‪Mr. Kim?

76
00:08:09,989 --> 00:08:10,865
‪Let's go.

77
00:08:31,511 --> 00:08:33,221
‪Are you really not going to tell us?

78
00:08:35,264 --> 00:08:36,390
‪Take him to a hospital.

79
00:08:37,183 --> 00:08:38,226
‪Okay.

80
00:08:58,287 --> 00:08:59,247
<i>‪I'm sorry.</i>

81
00:09:00,331 --> 00:09:01,290
<i>‪If you don't come…</i>

82
00:09:03,543 --> 00:09:04,669
<i>‪the kids will die.</i>

83
00:09:05,628 --> 00:09:06,587
<i>‪Please.</i>

84
00:09:07,338 --> 00:09:08,172
<i>‪I'm begging you.</i>

85
00:09:10,007 --> 00:09:11,175
‪I'll be right there.

86
00:09:19,809 --> 00:09:21,686
‪AGENT KIM REACTIVATED

87
00:09:21,769 --> 00:09:24,564
‪A FEW HOURS AGO

88
00:09:39,787 --> 00:09:40,746
‪Who are you?

89
00:09:42,665 --> 00:09:44,667
‪Damn it, I just mopped the floor.

90
00:09:46,502 --> 00:09:48,421
‪-It's him.
‪-This is a Taekwondo studio.

91
00:09:49,005 --> 00:09:50,423
‪Take off your shoes first.

92
00:10:00,516 --> 00:10:04,020
‪<i>-Whip it up, whip it up, up and down</i>
‪<i>-Whip it up</i>

93
00:10:04,103 --> 00:10:06,647
‪<i>-Whip it up, whip it up</i>
‪<i>-Whip it up</i>

94
00:10:07,398 --> 00:10:08,566
‪<i>Whip it…</i>

95
00:10:09,984 --> 00:10:11,068
‪What the hell?

96
00:10:11,694 --> 00:10:13,070
‪Are you Da-bin?

97
00:10:13,154 --> 00:10:14,363
‪Yes, that's me.

98
00:10:14,447 --> 00:10:15,448
‪Who are you?

99
00:10:24,498 --> 00:10:25,333
‪Take him.

100
00:10:31,297 --> 00:10:32,506
‪Mister.

101
00:10:32,590 --> 00:10:34,467
‪Why are you doing this to us?

102
00:10:35,176 --> 00:10:37,595
‪Please let us go.

103
00:10:37,678 --> 00:10:39,805
‪Untie us right now!

104
00:10:39,889 --> 00:10:40,890
‪Mister,

105
00:10:41,515 --> 00:10:43,184
‪please let us go.

106
00:10:44,727 --> 00:10:46,187
‪Please!

107
00:10:46,270 --> 00:10:47,772
‪JUHAK CONSTRUCTION CHAIRMAN JU GANG-CHAN

108
00:10:47,855 --> 00:10:49,148
<i>‪Ready, sir.</i>

109
00:11:55,756 --> 00:11:58,509
‪So you're willing to risk your life
‪for your friends' kids.

110
00:12:01,178 --> 00:12:02,346
‪I have to say I'm surprised.

111
00:12:49,560 --> 00:12:52,021
‪Then again, you two did the same.

112
00:12:56,650 --> 00:12:58,068
‪Now you get to choose.

113
00:13:00,529 --> 00:13:02,156
‪Will you kill your friend…

114
00:13:05,951 --> 00:13:07,161
‪or will you kill your kids?

115
00:13:24,637 --> 00:13:26,555
‪I'm really sorry…

116
00:13:30,851 --> 00:13:32,019
‪for dragging you into this.

117
00:13:36,649 --> 00:13:38,734
‪If 66 dies, the kids will live.

118
00:13:38,817 --> 00:13:40,027
‪Do you really have a choice?

119
00:13:58,379 --> 00:13:59,755
‪-No!
‪-Da-bin!

120
00:13:59,838 --> 00:14:00,839
‪-Stop!
‪-Da-bin!

121
00:14:00,923 --> 00:14:02,216
‪-Dad!
‪-Father!

122
00:14:02,299 --> 00:14:03,884
‪Dad, please help!

123
00:14:04,718 --> 00:14:05,636
‪Father…

124
00:14:05,719 --> 00:14:08,556
‪I'll do whatever you want, so stop it!

125
00:14:09,515 --> 00:14:10,474
‪Kim.

126
00:14:25,155 --> 00:14:26,323
‪Jin-cheol.

127
00:14:27,408 --> 00:14:28,284
‪Han-soo.

128
00:14:30,619 --> 00:14:31,912
‪You have to take me down…

129
00:14:34,832 --> 00:14:35,749
‪for the kids to live.

130
00:14:56,228 --> 00:14:57,479
‪Get it together!

131
00:15:05,738 --> 00:15:06,614
‪Get up.

132
00:15:10,117 --> 00:15:11,493
‪Kim!

133
00:15:12,494 --> 00:15:14,330
‪There must be a way.

134
00:15:18,167 --> 00:15:19,293
‪Focus on the kids.

135
00:15:20,794 --> 00:15:21,837
‪Focus!

136
00:15:38,854 --> 00:15:40,272
‪Han-soo!

137
00:16:05,214 --> 00:16:06,173
‪Kim.

138
00:16:25,901 --> 00:16:27,778
‪This is a bit of a letdown.

139
00:16:30,280 --> 00:16:32,324
‪You're not taking this seriously.

140
00:16:41,417 --> 00:16:42,793
‪I'll give you five minutes.

141
00:16:43,335 --> 00:16:45,004
‪If you don't kill him by then,

142
00:16:45,879 --> 00:16:47,715
‪I'll shoot the kids myself.

143
00:16:52,761 --> 00:16:54,263
‪Father!

144
00:16:54,346 --> 00:16:56,098
‪-Dad!
‪-Then I'll shoot 66.

145
00:16:56,181 --> 00:16:58,142
‪Please help!

146
00:16:58,225 --> 00:16:59,226
‪Father.

147
00:16:59,309 --> 00:17:01,478
‪-Dad!
‪-Father!

148
00:17:01,562 --> 00:17:03,272
‪-Father!
‪-Dad!

149
00:17:04,148 --> 00:17:05,065
‪Father…

150
00:17:07,192 --> 00:17:08,360
‪What are you waiting for?

151
00:17:11,697 --> 00:17:13,240
‪Your kids are calling for you.

152
00:17:17,119 --> 00:17:18,579
‪Dad!

153
00:17:18,662 --> 00:17:19,580
‪Dad!

154
00:17:21,040 --> 00:17:22,082
‪Dad!

155
00:17:26,503 --> 00:17:29,006
‪-Father!
‪-Dad!

156
00:17:49,318 --> 00:17:52,112
‪More, more, more!

157
00:18:02,706 --> 00:18:03,582
‪Get up.

158
00:18:03,665 --> 00:18:05,876
‪Get up! I said get up!

159
00:18:16,595 --> 00:18:17,513
‪Get up!

160
00:18:17,596 --> 00:18:19,056
‪Get up!

161
00:19:05,144 --> 00:19:06,228
‪Tae-hun…

162
00:19:08,105 --> 00:19:08,981
‪and Da-bin…

163
00:19:14,111 --> 00:19:15,195
‪You have to save them.

164
00:19:18,824 --> 00:19:19,700
‪And…

165
00:19:25,664 --> 00:19:26,707
‪please take care…

166
00:19:29,042 --> 00:19:30,085
‪of Min-ji.

167
00:19:45,559 --> 00:19:47,477
‪How sad,
‪you're going to miss Min-ji so much.

168
00:19:52,941 --> 00:19:53,901
<i>‪Come back.</i>

169
00:19:56,153 --> 00:19:57,237
‪I'll wait for you.

170
00:19:59,907 --> 00:20:01,200
<i>‪You'll come back.</i>

171
00:20:02,201 --> 00:20:03,410
‪You're my dad.

172
00:20:37,945 --> 00:20:38,820
<i>‪One.</i>

173
00:20:41,281 --> 00:20:42,241
<i>‪Two.</i>

174
00:20:44,910 --> 00:20:45,744
<i>‪Three.</i>

175
00:20:47,913 --> 00:20:49,414
‪-Dad!
‪-Uncle!

176
00:20:59,091 --> 00:20:59,925
<i>‪Four.</i>

177
00:21:01,301 --> 00:21:02,844
<i>‪-Damn it.</i>
‪-Get up.

178
00:21:02,928 --> 00:21:05,180
‪Get up! I said get up!

179
00:21:05,889 --> 00:21:06,848
‪Three seconds.

180
00:21:11,728 --> 00:21:13,146
‪Three seconds is enough.

181
00:21:29,246 --> 00:21:31,039
‪-Da-bin!
‪-Dad!

182
00:21:31,123 --> 00:21:33,208
‪-Da-bin!
‪-Dad!

183
00:21:33,959 --> 00:21:36,253
‪Dad, you got shot. Are you okay?

184
00:21:36,336 --> 00:21:38,755
‪-I'm okay. I didn't get shot.
‪-Are you okay?

185
00:21:38,839 --> 00:21:40,215
‪I'm fine.

186
00:21:40,299 --> 00:21:42,801
‪-I dodged it.
‪-Oh, you did?

187
00:21:42,884 --> 00:21:44,928
‪-You didn't get shot?
‪-No, I didn't.

188
00:21:45,012 --> 00:21:47,097
‪Are you okay? You must've been so scared.

189
00:21:47,180 --> 00:21:49,433
‪-My poor Da-bin!
‪-Dad, I'm fine.

190
00:21:49,516 --> 00:21:52,769
‪-If anything had happened to you…
‪-I said I'm fine!

191
00:21:52,853 --> 00:21:54,062
‪Hurry up and free me.

192
00:21:54,146 --> 00:21:55,897
‪Jeez, this is so annoying.

193
00:21:55,981 --> 00:21:57,774
‪-That hurts!
‪-Stop touching my hair!

194
00:21:57,858 --> 00:21:59,026
‪I won't touch your hair.

195
00:22:00,736 --> 00:22:02,487
‪You're okay, you're okay.

196
00:22:02,571 --> 00:22:04,072
‪Yeah, I'm fine.

197
00:22:04,156 --> 00:22:04,990
‪Let's go.

198
00:22:06,825 --> 00:22:07,784
‪Are you okay?

199
00:22:07,868 --> 00:22:09,870
‪-I'm fine.
‪-Can you get up?

200
00:22:13,123 --> 00:22:13,957
‪I'm okay.

201
00:22:15,751 --> 00:22:16,585
‪I'm fine.

202
00:22:23,884 --> 00:22:25,177
‪Kim!

203
00:22:30,265 --> 00:22:31,224
‪You okay?

204
00:22:32,017 --> 00:22:33,351
‪What about the kids?

205
00:22:33,435 --> 00:22:35,187
‪-They're fine.
‪-Are you okay?

206
00:22:35,270 --> 00:22:36,188
‪What do you think?

207
00:22:36,271 --> 00:22:37,397
‪Of course, he's not okay.

208
00:22:37,481 --> 00:22:39,357
‪Right, you got beaten up by us, after all.

209
00:22:39,441 --> 00:22:40,609
‪It took four seconds.

210
00:22:40,692 --> 00:22:42,277
‪That's why he got shot.

211
00:22:42,360 --> 00:22:44,112
‪It just grazed me.

212
00:22:44,196 --> 00:22:45,947
‪-You okay?
‪-What do you think?

213
00:22:46,031 --> 00:22:47,449
‪Of course, he's not okay.

214
00:22:51,870 --> 00:22:52,954
‪He seems okay.

215
00:22:56,500 --> 00:22:57,542
‪Hey, chairman.

216
00:22:59,086 --> 00:23:01,213
‪We have some unfinished business.

217
00:23:03,340 --> 00:23:04,674
‪A parent meeting.

218
00:23:14,601 --> 00:23:16,728
‪What else is there to do?

219
00:23:17,437 --> 00:23:18,647
‪I have to keep my promise.

220
00:23:20,190 --> 00:23:21,775
‪Are you okay to drive?

221
00:23:21,858 --> 00:23:23,276
‪I guess he is.

222
00:23:40,127 --> 00:23:41,628
‪What about the kids?

223
00:23:41,711 --> 00:23:44,256
‪Shouldn't we keep an eye on them
‪so they don't go out?

224
00:23:44,339 --> 00:23:45,757
‪Does Tae-hun ever listen to you?

225
00:23:45,841 --> 00:23:47,259
‪Of course, he doesn't.

226
00:23:47,342 --> 00:23:50,220
‪He even attacks his own father.

227
00:23:51,805 --> 00:23:54,850
‪At least Da-bin doesn't attack me.

228
00:23:54,933 --> 00:23:56,101
‪She just ignores me.

229
00:23:57,936 --> 00:23:59,855
‪We should leave them with someone
‪who can intimidate them.

230
00:24:00,772 --> 00:24:02,274
‪-Like who?
‪-I know someone.

231
00:24:02,357 --> 00:24:03,775
‪Someone scarier than me.

232
00:24:03,859 --> 00:24:07,737
‪Actually, they might be
‪the scariest person on the planet.

233
00:24:09,322 --> 00:24:10,157
‪Let's go.

234
00:24:14,119 --> 00:24:15,120
‪Man, my legs.

235
00:24:16,288 --> 00:24:17,330
‪My poor legs.

236
00:24:18,707 --> 00:24:20,125
‪My legs are killing me.

237
00:24:23,336 --> 00:24:24,504
‪My steering wheel!

238
00:24:26,631 --> 00:24:28,091
‪Come on!

239
00:24:31,970 --> 00:24:34,389
‪SECURITY COMMANDER KANG JI-YEONG

240
00:24:39,311 --> 00:24:40,562
‪Is this a joke?

241
00:24:40,645 --> 00:24:43,315
‪17TH AMPHIBIOUS MOBILE BRIGADE
‪RED DRAGON UNIT SPECIAL SECURITY BATTALION

242
00:24:43,899 --> 00:24:44,733
‪Honey…

243
00:24:46,735 --> 00:24:49,196
‪Would you mind
‪watching the kids for a bit?

244
00:24:50,030 --> 00:24:52,741
‪If you could keep them in a room

245
00:24:52,824 --> 00:24:54,326
‪and protect them for a few days…

246
00:24:56,203 --> 00:24:58,288
‪Please?

247
00:24:59,289 --> 00:25:00,332
‪Please?

248
00:25:04,127 --> 00:25:06,671
‪This isn't a daycare center.

249
00:25:07,964 --> 00:25:08,840
‪You little punk!

250
00:25:10,592 --> 00:25:12,886
‪This is fake. Do you have any guns, lady?

251
00:25:12,969 --> 00:25:15,222
‪I told you not to call me that.

252
00:25:15,722 --> 00:25:16,890
‪Be quiet and go away.

253
00:25:19,351 --> 00:25:20,644
‪Mom, lend me your phone.

254
00:25:21,269 --> 00:25:22,270
‪Da-bin, be quiet.

255
00:25:25,232 --> 00:25:27,442
‪I told you not to get into trouble.

256
00:25:27,525 --> 00:25:28,818
‪I didn't get into trouble.

257
00:25:28,902 --> 00:25:31,071
‪I just felt so bad for Kim
‪that I had no choice but to help.

258
00:25:31,154 --> 00:25:33,698
‪I had no choice
‪because Jin-cheol told me to help.

259
00:25:34,491 --> 00:25:36,451
‪Kim? Again?

260
00:25:36,534 --> 00:25:38,078
‪I ought to just…

261
00:25:38,161 --> 00:25:39,037
‪That's not true.

262
00:25:41,706 --> 00:25:42,749
‪It's not true, honey.

263
00:25:44,084 --> 00:25:45,460
‪I wanted to help him.

264
00:25:46,378 --> 00:25:47,212
‪It was my choice.

265
00:25:48,255 --> 00:25:49,130
‪My friend…

266
00:25:50,590 --> 00:25:53,385
‪had to do one last mission
‪to see his daughter again.

267
00:25:55,220 --> 00:25:56,429
‪So I wanted to help him.

268
00:25:58,473 --> 00:25:59,307
‪Me too.

269
00:26:11,069 --> 00:26:13,947
‪Still, you shouldn't have
‪put the kids in danger.

270
00:26:15,740 --> 00:26:16,574
‪I'm sorry, honey.

271
00:26:16,658 --> 00:26:18,285
‪I'm sorry too.

272
00:26:22,330 --> 00:26:23,665
‪The kids will stay with me.

273
00:26:24,958 --> 00:26:26,501
‪I can't trust you two.

274
00:26:26,584 --> 00:26:27,794
‪-Honey!
‪-Honey!

275
00:26:27,877 --> 00:26:28,712
‪I mean, Ji-yeong.

276
00:26:30,171 --> 00:26:33,341
‪When will you middle-aged men grow up?

277
00:26:33,425 --> 00:26:35,468
‪Seriously, when will you…

278
00:26:36,303 --> 00:26:37,137
‪When…

279
00:26:38,555 --> 00:26:39,389
‪Honey.

280
00:26:39,472 --> 00:26:41,683
‪Have I told you

281
00:26:41,766 --> 00:26:42,767
‪-that I love--
‪-Get out.

282
00:26:42,851 --> 00:26:43,768
‪-Yes, he has.
‪-Let's go.

283
00:26:43,852 --> 00:26:45,103
‪-Hurry.
‪-Sit properly.

284
00:26:45,854 --> 00:26:48,064
‪Eat as much as you can in one sitting,
‪and don't ask for snacks.

285
00:26:48,148 --> 00:26:49,774
‪-You know what to do, right?
‪-What?

286
00:26:49,858 --> 00:26:51,901
‪And don't ask
‪for the Wi-Fi password, okay?

287
00:26:51,985 --> 00:26:54,070
‪-Why?
‪-Don't ask. Just be quiet.

288
00:26:54,154 --> 00:26:55,989
‪-Got it?
‪-Yeah, just go already.

289
00:26:56,072 --> 00:26:57,615
‪-Don't make her mad.
‪-Okay, okay.

290
00:26:57,699 --> 00:26:58,992
‪All right, attention!

291
00:26:59,075 --> 00:26:59,909
‪Salute!

292
00:27:01,494 --> 00:27:02,329
‪Hands down.

293
00:27:03,913 --> 00:27:04,748
‪Dad.

294
00:27:04,831 --> 00:27:05,707
‪Do as she says.

295
00:27:11,921 --> 00:27:12,839
‪Are you hungry?

296
00:27:15,133 --> 00:27:15,967
‪Yes, I am.

297
00:27:16,593 --> 00:27:19,137
‪Those guys didn't even feed you?

298
00:27:19,220 --> 00:27:21,681
‪What do you want?
‪Want me to order <i>‪jjajangmyeon</i>‪?

299
00:27:24,768 --> 00:27:31,608
‪INTER-KOREAN GOVERNMENT TALKS

300
00:27:34,944 --> 00:27:37,989
‪I'm pleased that both sides
‪could come to an agreement.

301
00:27:38,573 --> 00:27:40,283
‪I hope that the North and the South

302
00:27:40,367 --> 00:27:43,203
‪can move toward a cooperative future
‪through the free-trade zone.

303
00:27:43,286 --> 00:27:44,120
‪Likewise.

304
00:27:46,122 --> 00:27:47,916
‪Thank you, everyone.

305
00:27:49,417 --> 00:27:51,920
‪Can the two of you please shake hands?

306
00:28:00,595 --> 00:28:03,807
‪I think we have other matters to discuss.

307
00:28:05,016 --> 00:28:06,768
‪About what happened last night, that is.

308
00:28:21,282 --> 00:28:22,450
‪As you know,

309
00:28:23,159 --> 00:28:27,747
‪we've done our best to accommodate
‪the North's requests during this visit.

310
00:28:28,706 --> 00:28:29,541
‪Don't you agree?

311
00:28:29,624 --> 00:28:33,461
‪It was all for the good
‪of inter-Korean cooperation.

312
00:28:34,129 --> 00:28:36,923
‪What are your thoughts, sir?

313
00:28:39,467 --> 00:28:40,385
‪But you know,

314
00:28:41,636 --> 00:28:46,099
‪I think what happened last night
‪was out of line.

315
00:28:46,182 --> 00:28:47,684
‪Shouldn't you take responsibility

316
00:28:48,518 --> 00:28:52,522
‪for causing such a scene
‪on South Korean soil?

317
00:28:52,605 --> 00:28:53,773
‪That was…

318
00:28:57,110 --> 00:28:58,570
‪There was an internal issue.

319
00:28:58,653 --> 00:28:59,821
‪And that issue

320
00:28:59,904 --> 00:29:02,323
‪almost turned South Korea
‪into a battlefield.

321
00:29:02,407 --> 00:29:04,409
‪No, we had no intention of--

322
00:29:04,492 --> 00:29:05,618
‪Now, now.

323
00:29:09,956 --> 00:29:11,916
‪Considering the outcome of these talks,

324
00:29:12,834 --> 00:29:18,757
‪we won't take official retaliatory action
‪against the North.

325
00:29:19,507 --> 00:29:20,675
‪However,

326
00:29:20,759 --> 00:29:23,636
‪let's settle this with the understanding

327
00:29:24,596 --> 00:29:27,891
‪that we have zero responsibility
‪for the casualties on your side.

328
00:29:32,854 --> 00:29:33,772
‪Understood.

329
00:29:34,439 --> 00:29:39,486
‪WE WELCOME THE NORTH KOREAN DELEGATION
‪TO JUHAK HERITAGE RESORT

330
00:29:55,668 --> 00:29:56,836
‪Listen carefully.

331
00:29:57,921 --> 00:30:01,716
‪The Party will be told that Ri Eung Ryeong
‪and 66 have been summarily executed.

332
00:30:02,759 --> 00:30:06,888
‪If word gets out that we lost them
‪after the South handed them over to us,

333
00:30:06,971 --> 00:30:10,600
‪we're all going to have to
‪take responsibility.

334
00:30:12,602 --> 00:30:14,813
‪I've already spoken
‪with the delegation officials,

335
00:30:15,522 --> 00:30:17,190
‪so make sure to keep your men quiet.

336
00:30:17,816 --> 00:30:18,650
‪Understand?

337
00:30:19,275 --> 00:30:20,276
‪Yes, sir.

338
00:30:29,744 --> 00:30:31,663
‪-What are you talking about?
‪-Over there.

339
00:30:32,413 --> 00:30:34,332
‪That's a person, right?

340
00:30:34,415 --> 00:30:35,333
‪-What the heck?
‪-What is that?

341
00:30:35,416 --> 00:30:36,960
‪That's a person, for crying out loud!

342
00:30:37,043 --> 00:30:39,754
‪-Contact EMS and call for backup.
‪-Yes, sir.

343
00:30:39,838 --> 00:30:41,589
‪-Sir, stay right here.
‪-Okay.

344
00:30:41,673 --> 00:30:43,967
‪MYEONGJIN CENTRAL HOSPITAL

345
00:30:47,220 --> 00:30:48,680
‪VIP1
‪UNIDENTIFIED PERSON

346
00:31:28,511 --> 00:31:30,889
‪Goodness, Director General.

347
00:31:32,098 --> 00:31:33,308
‪How do you feel?

348
00:31:33,892 --> 00:31:34,809
‪I'm fine.

349
00:31:45,778 --> 00:31:46,946
‪Start recording.

350
00:31:50,408 --> 00:31:51,492
‪What's the rush?

351
00:31:53,202 --> 00:31:54,495
‪Quickly, quickly.

352
00:31:54,579 --> 00:31:56,039
‪This is how it is in the South.

353
00:31:56,122 --> 00:31:57,290
‪You should get used to it too.

354
00:31:58,666 --> 00:32:00,418
‪All right, then.

355
00:32:00,501 --> 00:32:03,046
‪Let's start with the status of the ICBMs.

356
00:32:05,548 --> 00:32:08,009
‪I have one last condition.

357
00:32:09,510 --> 00:32:10,345
‪A condition?

358
00:32:12,847 --> 00:32:16,059
‪After I give you all the information,

359
00:32:16,643 --> 00:32:20,480
‪send me to Macau for asylum.

360
00:32:24,442 --> 00:32:25,693
‪I'll think about it

361
00:32:26,277 --> 00:32:28,071
‪depending on the quality
‪of the information.

362
00:32:30,823 --> 00:32:34,285
‪So our understanding
‪is that the Strategic Rocket Force

363
00:32:34,369 --> 00:32:36,162
‪is structured around a three-axis system.

364
00:32:36,245 --> 00:32:38,498
‪Cholsan County, North Pyongan Province.

365
00:32:38,581 --> 00:32:40,291
‪Chonchon County, Chagang Province.

366
00:32:40,375 --> 00:32:43,086
‪And Kilju County, North Hamgyong Province.

367
00:32:43,169 --> 00:32:48,174
‪At least 12 transporter erector launchers
‪are currently in service.

368
00:32:49,217 --> 00:32:51,552
‪What about the current range?

369
00:32:51,636 --> 00:32:53,471
‪Not only can they easily reach Guam,

370
00:32:54,430 --> 00:32:56,516
‪but Alaska

371
00:32:56,599 --> 00:33:00,478
‪and the US West Coast
‪are also within striking range.

372
00:33:01,562 --> 00:33:05,441
‪How are they handling the fuel transition?

373
00:33:05,525 --> 00:33:07,860
‪It's liquid-based right now,

374
00:33:07,944 --> 00:33:13,157
‪but they're currently transitioning over
‪to solid fuel.

375
00:33:14,200 --> 00:33:16,786
‪That's why I'm needed.

376
00:33:16,869 --> 00:33:19,414
‪You see, all the information

377
00:33:19,998 --> 00:33:21,499
‪is right in here.

378
00:33:52,321 --> 00:33:57,285
‪VIP1
‪UNIDENTIFIED PERSON

379
00:35:13,528 --> 00:35:18,741
‪PATIENT TRANSPORT

380
00:35:26,999 --> 00:35:28,668
‪You kept your promise.

381
00:35:29,418 --> 00:35:30,628
‪What are you going to do?

382
00:35:32,547 --> 00:35:33,631
‪I'll take it from here.

383
00:35:34,215 --> 00:35:37,176
‪It'd be a shame
‪to finish off an enemy so easily.

384
00:36:01,659 --> 00:36:04,036
‪I need you to do one last thing for me.

385
00:36:04,120 --> 00:36:05,621
‪No matter what happens,

386
00:36:05,705 --> 00:36:08,416
‪promise me you'll survive.

387
00:36:13,045 --> 00:36:13,880
‪What are you doing?

388
00:36:15,798 --> 00:36:16,924
‪If you're done, go.

389
00:36:27,226 --> 00:36:28,186
‪I wish you and your daughter…

390
00:36:30,563 --> 00:36:31,439
‪a good life.

391
00:36:36,736 --> 00:36:37,904
‪I'll stay alive too.

392
00:36:40,990 --> 00:36:41,824
‪Good.

393
00:36:43,117 --> 00:36:43,951
‪Stay alive…

394
00:36:46,954 --> 00:36:48,039
‪no matter what.

395
00:37:11,729 --> 00:37:13,147
‪COMMANDER'S OFFICE
‪CHEONSAN UNIT

396
00:37:13,856 --> 00:37:14,690
‪So?

397
00:37:15,316 --> 00:37:17,652
‪Who kidnapped Ri Eung Ryeong?

398
00:37:17,735 --> 00:37:20,196
‪We have yet to identify the suspect, sir.

399
00:37:20,821 --> 00:37:22,198
‪We're currently analyzing CCTV footage,

400
00:37:22,782 --> 00:37:24,617
‪and we'll mobilize a team
‪once we track their movements.

401
00:37:24,700 --> 00:37:26,702
‪Forget it. Let it go.

402
00:37:27,245 --> 00:37:28,079
‪Sir?

403
00:37:28,162 --> 00:37:30,706
‪We got all the information
‪we needed out of him.

404
00:37:31,499 --> 00:37:34,961
‪It'd be a waste of taxpayer money
‪to keep him around longer.

405
00:37:36,420 --> 00:37:37,296
‪It doesn't matter

406
00:37:37,380 --> 00:37:39,882
‪whether he smuggles himself
‪out of the country or drops dead.

407
00:37:40,508 --> 00:37:42,677
‪Either way, it's for the better.

408
00:37:43,302 --> 00:37:44,345
‪But still…

409
00:37:44,428 --> 00:37:45,596
‪Just do as I say.

410
00:37:46,764 --> 00:37:47,682
‪That's an order.

411
00:38:32,018 --> 00:38:32,977
‪Is this Macau?

412
00:38:47,033 --> 00:38:47,950
‪Shit.

413
00:39:06,802 --> 00:39:07,720
‪THE SEAS OF OUR HOMELAND
‪DO NOT TOLERATE LIES

414
00:39:07,803 --> 00:39:08,763
‪THE COASTLINE IS THE FRONT LINE
‪OF NATIONAL DEFENSE!

415
00:39:10,598 --> 00:39:12,016
‪No, it can't be.

416
00:39:15,186 --> 00:39:16,270
‪F****** hell!

417
00:39:16,354 --> 00:39:17,605
‪Don't move!

418
00:39:17,688 --> 00:39:19,148
‪Stay right there!

419
00:39:21,525 --> 00:39:22,693
‪-Stop!
‪-Stop right there!

420
00:39:23,944 --> 00:39:24,987
‪Stop!

421
00:39:26,822 --> 00:39:28,115
‪Stop right there!

422
00:39:37,249 --> 00:39:42,296
‪JUHAK CONSTRUCTION CO., LTD.

423
00:39:42,880 --> 00:39:44,340
‪CHO PYEONG-GYEON

424
00:40:03,692 --> 00:40:04,527
<i>‪It's me, sir.</i>

425
00:40:04,610 --> 00:40:05,569
‪Hey.

426
00:40:06,153 --> 00:40:08,656
<i>‪My goodness. Are you alive and well?</i>

427
00:40:08,739 --> 00:40:11,992
‪What made you call me all of a sudden?

428
00:40:12,076 --> 00:40:14,078
‪I called to ask you a favor.

429
00:40:14,829 --> 00:40:15,663
‪A favor?

430
00:40:16,455 --> 00:40:17,415
‪What is it?

431
00:40:18,999 --> 00:40:19,959
‪I need you to dissolve

432
00:40:20,793 --> 00:40:22,378
‪Juhak Construction.

433
00:40:23,045 --> 00:40:24,088
‪Goodness.

434
00:40:24,171 --> 00:40:26,257
‪You haven't called in over a decade,

435
00:40:26,340 --> 00:40:28,008
‪and that's what you ask me for?

436
00:40:28,592 --> 00:40:30,177
‪It has to do with my daughter.

437
00:40:30,803 --> 00:40:31,929
‪Please, sir.

438
00:40:32,012 --> 00:40:35,057
‪My goodness, that poor thing.

439
00:40:35,141 --> 00:40:36,100
‪Good heavens.

440
00:40:36,183 --> 00:40:38,227
‪She must be really big now.

441
00:40:38,811 --> 00:40:40,438
<i>‪She's pretty like her mom, right?</i>

442
00:40:41,105 --> 00:40:42,982
<i>‪I understand.</i>

443
00:40:43,065 --> 00:40:45,359
‪I've known her since she was born, so…

444
00:40:47,236 --> 00:40:48,904
‪Juhak Construction, huh?

445
00:40:50,698 --> 00:40:51,574
‪All right.

446
00:40:52,199 --> 00:40:53,242
‪You got it.

447
00:40:55,119 --> 00:40:56,078
‪Thank you.

448
00:40:56,162 --> 00:40:58,414
<i>‪Just wait a few days.</i>

449
00:40:58,998 --> 00:41:00,708
<i>‪Juhak Construction is nothing.</i>

450
00:41:00,791 --> 00:41:04,044
‪I'll chop it up like a cucumber

451
00:41:04,128 --> 00:41:06,255
‪and make a salad out of it.

452
00:41:06,922 --> 00:41:08,924
<i>‪You know this will cost you, right?</i>

453
00:41:09,467 --> 00:41:14,221
‪We're close, but we're professionals,
‪so I won't lower my fees.

454
00:41:14,889 --> 00:41:16,098
<i>‪You understand, right?</i>

455
00:41:16,182 --> 00:41:17,892
‪-Yes, I do.
<i>‪-Good.</i>

456
00:41:17,975 --> 00:41:19,143
<i>‪All right, then.</i>

457
00:41:19,226 --> 00:41:20,478
<i>‪I'll call you back.</i>

458
00:41:21,270 --> 00:41:22,480
‪Thank you, sir.

459
00:41:36,243 --> 00:41:38,496
<i>‪Prosecutors have conducted</i>
<i>‪a surprise search and seizure</i>

460
00:41:38,579 --> 00:41:43,083
<i>‪at Juhak Construction headquarters</i>
<i>‪and its affiliates earlier this morning.</i>

461
00:41:43,167 --> 00:41:44,668
‪-What's your business here?
<i>‪-The investigation team</i>

462
00:41:44,752 --> 00:41:47,421
‪-We have a search and seizure warrant.
<i>‪-is looking into suspicious cash flows</i>

463
00:41:47,505 --> 00:41:51,300
<i>‪of tens of billions of won</i>
<i>‪between Juhak Construction affiliates</i>

464
00:41:51,383 --> 00:41:52,593
<i>‪and political figures.</i>

465
00:41:53,219 --> 00:41:56,138
<i>‪The said team believes the repeated,</i>
<i>‪large-scale fund transfers</i>

466
00:41:56,222 --> 00:41:59,475
<i>‪were not legitimate business transactions</i>

467
00:41:59,558 --> 00:42:02,561
<i>‪and is now tracing their source</i>
<i>‪and where they were ultimately used.</i>

468
00:42:03,729 --> 00:42:07,149
<i>‪This investigation</i>
<i>‪was reportedly triggered</i>

469
00:42:07,233 --> 00:42:09,360
<i>‪after the Financial Intelligence Unit</i>

470
00:42:09,443 --> 00:42:12,571
<i>‪filed suspicious transaction reports</i>
<i>‪with the prosecution late last year.</i>

471
00:42:12,655 --> 00:42:14,365
‪Do you acknowledge the bribery charges?

472
00:42:14,448 --> 00:42:16,158
‪Are the claims of redevelopment bias true?

473
00:42:16,242 --> 00:42:17,868
‪-Please answer, Assemblyman!
‪-Let me pass.

474
00:42:17,952 --> 00:42:19,537
‪-Please comment!
‪-We can do this another time.

475
00:42:43,102 --> 00:42:44,853
‪Are you going on a trip abroad

476
00:42:45,354 --> 00:42:47,189
‪after selling out your country?

477
00:42:49,400 --> 00:42:50,818
‪-Arrest him.
‪-Yes, sir.

478
00:42:54,446 --> 00:42:55,864
‪Let go of me!

479
00:42:56,490 --> 00:42:57,324
‪Let go!

480
00:43:01,745 --> 00:43:03,038
‪CAMBODIA

481
00:43:03,122 --> 00:43:05,332
<i>‪A court has issued an arrest warrant</i>

482
00:43:05,416 --> 00:43:08,502
<i>‪for Chairman Ju Gang-chan</i>
<i>‪of Juhak Construction</i>

483
00:43:08,586 --> 00:43:11,088
<i>‪on charges of kidnapping, murder,</i>
<i>‪and threatening national security.</i>

484
00:43:11,171 --> 00:43:13,173
<i>‪The court cited the severity of the crimes</i>

485
00:43:13,257 --> 00:43:16,010
<i>‪and the risk of evidence tampering</i>
<i>‪for its decision.</i>

486
00:43:16,093 --> 00:43:19,722
<i>‪Chairman Ju</i>
<i>‪is reportedly hospitalized in Seoul.</i>

487
00:43:19,805 --> 00:43:21,515
<i>‪Meanwhile, the prosecution has stated</i>

488
00:43:21,599 --> 00:43:23,350
<i>‪it'll expand the investigation to include</i>

489
00:43:23,434 --> 00:43:26,061
<i>‪the company's founding history</i>
<i>‪and the chairman's illegal activities.</i>

490
00:43:28,522 --> 00:43:30,316
<i>‪Hye-ri, I know what you did.</i>

491
00:43:30,399 --> 00:43:31,233
‪<i>Do you know Kim Min-ji?</i>

492
00:43:31,317 --> 00:43:33,068
<i>‪Dang, the police came by the school.</i>

493
00:43:33,152 --> 00:43:35,112
<i>‪-I heard his daughter left the country.</i>
<i>‪-Daughter of a murderer.</i>

494
00:43:35,195 --> 00:43:37,031
<i>‪-Interpol is after you too.</i>
<i>‪-She's going to prison with her dad.</i>

495
00:43:37,114 --> 00:43:38,157
<i>‪Ju Hye-ri is screwed.</i>

496
00:43:51,795 --> 00:43:52,671
‪He's coming out!

497
00:43:55,424 --> 00:43:57,343
‪When did you start making contact
‪with North Korea?

498
00:43:57,426 --> 00:43:59,094
‪Are the murder allegations true?

499
00:43:59,178 --> 00:44:02,139
‪Are you aware that your daughter,
‪who fled abroad, has been arrested?

500
00:44:04,099 --> 00:44:05,726
‪-Please say something!
‪-A comment, please!

501
00:44:05,809 --> 00:44:06,977
‪Say something, asshole.

502
00:44:12,483 --> 00:44:13,317
‪How've you been?

503
00:44:25,579 --> 00:44:27,414
‪How does it feel
‪to get taken down by a dog?

504
00:44:28,374 --> 00:44:31,794
‪You pulled out my teeth,
‪but I still have my claws, you bastard!

505
00:44:47,059 --> 00:44:50,020
‪You should've returned
‪as soon as the mission was over.

506
00:44:51,230 --> 00:44:52,981
‪Where have you been

507
00:44:54,274 --> 00:44:55,526
‪looking like that?

508
00:44:58,529 --> 00:45:00,614
‪Didn't you miss your daughter?

509
00:45:03,450 --> 00:45:07,037
‪I had some business to take care of
‪for Min-ji's sake.

510
00:45:09,164 --> 00:45:09,998
‪So?

511
00:45:10,624 --> 00:45:11,875
‪Is the business taken care of?

512
00:45:15,295 --> 00:45:16,130
‪Yes.

513
00:45:18,298 --> 00:45:20,634
‪It's all over now.

514
00:45:22,469 --> 00:45:25,139
‪Then it's time for me
‪to wrap things up as well.

515
00:45:26,098 --> 00:45:27,141
‪Number 66…

516
00:45:30,310 --> 00:45:31,311
‪must die.

517
00:45:37,192 --> 00:45:41,071
<i>‪The body of a man with a gunshot wound</i>
<i>‪was discovered by an herb collector</i>

518
00:45:41,155 --> 00:45:43,323
<i>‪in the woods near the resort</i>

519
00:45:43,407 --> 00:45:45,868
<i>‪where the North Korean delegation</i>
<i>‪was staying.</i>

520
00:45:45,951 --> 00:45:49,037
<i>‪The deceased has been identified</i>
<i>‪as a man in his forties, surnamed Kim,</i>

521
00:45:49,121 --> 00:45:53,500
<i>‪and police have launched an investigation</i>
<i>‪into the exact circumstances of his death.</i>

522
00:45:55,794 --> 00:45:57,713
‪BODY WITH GUNSHOT WOUND DISCOVERED
‪NEAR NORTH KOREAN DELEGATION LODGING

523
00:45:59,339 --> 00:46:00,841
‪DECEASED IDENTIFIED AS MAN IN HIS FORTIES
‪INVESTIGATION UNDERWAY

524
00:46:19,902 --> 00:46:21,111
‪HIGH-PROFILE WANTED FUGITIVE
‪COMPREHENSIVE PROFILE

525
00:46:21,195 --> 00:46:22,863
‪YOUNGER YEARS
‪ESTIMATED CURRENT APPEARANCE

526
00:46:23,906 --> 00:46:25,782
‪DELETE THIS PROFILE?
‪NO / YES

527
00:46:52,017 --> 00:46:53,393
‪THE LATE KIM, THE LATE IM YU-JIN

528
00:47:46,822 --> 00:47:47,823
‪I'm back.

529
00:47:53,287 --> 00:47:55,872
‪I'm not going to run into your arms.

530
00:47:56,957 --> 00:47:58,125
‪That'd be too cheesy.

531
00:48:01,461 --> 00:48:02,462
‪You knew?

532
00:48:03,046 --> 00:48:04,715
‪Sang-a told me.

533
00:48:06,258 --> 00:48:07,759
‪She said you died.

534
00:48:09,845 --> 00:48:11,638
‪But that you'd come back alive.

535
00:48:26,278 --> 00:48:27,195
‪I promise

536
00:48:28,739 --> 00:48:30,073
‪never to leave you again.

537
00:48:32,576 --> 00:48:33,410
‪I'll always…

538
00:48:35,329 --> 00:48:37,664
‪be right by your side.

539
00:48:44,504 --> 00:48:45,380
‪Dad…

540
00:48:48,050 --> 00:48:50,552
‪Do you know how worried I was?

541
00:48:51,595 --> 00:48:54,431
‪I was so afraid
‪something had happened to you.

542
00:48:58,935 --> 00:49:01,146
‪Thank you for coming back.

543
00:49:13,200 --> 00:49:14,117
‪It's okay.

544
00:49:17,454 --> 00:49:19,164
‪Wow, the flowers are so pretty.

545
00:49:21,708 --> 00:49:23,418
‪I should come visit Mom more often.

546
00:49:25,629 --> 00:49:27,130
‪Did Mom like flowers too?

547
00:49:27,964 --> 00:49:28,799
‪Yeah.

548
00:49:30,384 --> 00:49:31,635
‪Maybe that's why I'm pretty.

549
00:49:32,260 --> 00:49:33,095
‪No.

550
00:49:33,804 --> 00:49:34,763
‪You're pretty

551
00:49:35,639 --> 00:49:37,057
‪because you take after your mom.

552
00:49:38,266 --> 00:49:39,101
‪You're right.

553
00:49:39,184 --> 00:49:40,977
‪I definitely don't get my looks from you.

554
00:49:41,603 --> 00:49:42,437
‪Jeez.

555
00:49:43,939 --> 00:49:45,649
‪What happens to us now?

556
00:49:47,984 --> 00:49:49,111
‪From now on,

557
00:49:50,070 --> 00:49:52,239
‪we're going to live completely new lives.

558
00:49:53,031 --> 00:49:55,575
‪We'll live in a new place
‪with new identities.

559
00:49:55,659 --> 00:49:56,660
‪We'll even have new names.

560
00:49:57,577 --> 00:49:58,412
‪I see.

561
00:50:01,665 --> 00:50:04,000
‪But I still want you to call me Min-ji.

562
00:50:04,084 --> 00:50:05,919
‪Why? You don't want to change your name?

563
00:50:06,002 --> 00:50:07,587
‪Mom gave me that name.

564
00:50:11,591 --> 00:50:12,759
‪Okay, I will.

565
00:50:13,969 --> 00:50:16,304
‪It feels like
‪we have our own little secret.

566
00:50:16,388 --> 00:50:17,222
‪Doesn't it?

567
00:50:21,017 --> 00:50:23,729
‪It won't be easy starting a new life.

568
00:50:24,354 --> 00:50:25,188
‪Will you be okay?

569
00:50:27,357 --> 00:50:28,775
‪I think it'll be fun.

570
00:50:30,777 --> 00:50:33,155
‪This life wasn't much fun anyway.

571
00:50:33,989 --> 00:50:35,407
‪I'll just consider this a new beginning.

572
00:50:40,620 --> 00:50:43,582
‪Then how about a new beginning
‪as a model student?

573
00:50:44,249 --> 00:50:46,042
‪You can study hard and go to college.

574
00:50:46,668 --> 00:50:47,753
‪What?

575
00:50:47,836 --> 00:50:49,337
‪Why do you get to decide that?

576
00:50:50,005 --> 00:50:52,299
‪You don't even know what I want to become.

577
00:50:52,382 --> 00:50:53,842
‪I can start learning now.

578
00:50:56,470 --> 00:50:58,180
‪What do you want to be, Min-ji?

579
00:51:00,056 --> 00:51:00,891
‪Me?

580
00:51:02,142 --> 00:51:03,018
‪Maybe a singer?

581
00:51:11,359 --> 00:51:12,277
‪What?

582
00:51:13,945 --> 00:51:15,781
‪If you take after me,
‪singing isn't your thing.

583
00:51:16,364 --> 00:51:18,283
‪What do you mean?

584
00:51:18,366 --> 00:51:20,243
‪I'm tone-deaf!

585
00:51:24,998 --> 00:51:25,832
‪Is that funny?

586
00:51:26,875 --> 00:51:28,210
‪My gosh.

587
00:51:32,380 --> 00:51:33,298
‪Mr. Kim.

588
00:51:34,800 --> 00:51:35,967
‪And Min-ji.

589
00:51:39,095 --> 00:51:40,555
‪Those are your new identities.

590
00:51:40,639 --> 00:51:43,141
‪There's a manual inside the file,
‪so learn it inside and out.

591
00:51:44,017 --> 00:51:45,185
‪Especially you, Min-ji.

592
00:51:54,778 --> 00:51:56,446
‪"Kim Ji-min"?

593
00:51:58,532 --> 00:52:00,283
‪You didn't even bother trying, did you?

594
00:52:00,367 --> 00:52:03,286
‪Well, coming up with new names
‪isn't our job.

595
00:52:06,206 --> 00:52:07,457
‪Thank you.

596
00:52:12,045 --> 00:52:14,422
‪I hope I never see your face again.

597
00:52:16,550 --> 00:52:17,634
‪Likewise.

598
00:52:18,593 --> 00:52:21,596
‪I don't really want to
‪see your face either.

599
00:52:21,680 --> 00:52:22,806
‪Me too.

600
00:52:22,889 --> 00:52:23,723
‪What?

601
00:52:26,434 --> 00:52:28,770
‪I've never seen you smile before, Mr. Kim.

602
00:52:29,437 --> 00:52:31,064
‪This is him cracking up.

603
00:52:31,147 --> 00:52:32,524
‪-Really?
‪-Yeah.

604
00:52:35,485 --> 00:52:36,486
‪Here.

605
00:52:38,071 --> 00:52:39,197
‪What is it?

606
00:52:40,824 --> 00:52:43,577
‪I hope you grow up to be
‪someone great and admirable.

607
00:52:50,250 --> 00:52:51,793
‪I guess it's kind of pretty.

608
00:52:52,419 --> 00:52:53,253
‪Thank you.

609
00:52:55,297 --> 00:52:57,507
‪He's much warmer than he seems.

610
00:52:59,009 --> 00:53:00,969
‪We chose that together.

611
00:53:01,052 --> 00:53:02,512
‪The three of you bought a single hairpin?

612
00:53:02,596 --> 00:53:03,597
‪It's an expensive one.

613
00:53:07,434 --> 00:53:08,977
‪-Do you like it?
‪-Yeah.

614
00:53:09,561 --> 00:53:11,104
‪-Get back to work.
‪-Right.

615
00:53:11,187 --> 00:53:12,272
‪-Yes, sir.
‪-Yes, sir.

616
00:53:22,198 --> 00:53:23,199
‪Mr. Kim!

617
00:53:24,117 --> 00:53:25,285
‪Kim!

618
00:53:27,871 --> 00:53:29,039
‪Take this.

619
00:53:29,998 --> 00:53:30,916
‪It's not much.

620
00:53:30,999 --> 00:53:32,500
‪It's to prevent bad luck.

621
00:53:33,251 --> 00:53:37,172
‪I thought a new suit would be fitting
‪for your fresh start.

622
00:53:37,797 --> 00:53:39,925
‪Wow, you're so lucky, Dad.

623
00:53:40,008 --> 00:53:42,510
‪Come on, take it. It's heavy.

624
00:53:42,594 --> 00:53:43,637
‪Thank you.

625
00:53:43,720 --> 00:53:47,349
‪Iron out the wrinkles in your suit,

626
00:53:47,432 --> 00:53:49,809
‪and the wrinkles in life
‪will iron themselves out.

627
00:53:51,728 --> 00:53:52,646
‪I'll remember that.

628
00:53:52,729 --> 00:53:56,441
‪Goodness, I wonder
‪when I'll get to see you again.

629
00:53:57,734 --> 00:53:58,777
‪By the way,

630
00:53:59,402 --> 00:54:01,988
‪we lived in the same neighborhood

631
00:54:02,072 --> 00:54:03,865
‪but never even knew each other's names.

632
00:54:05,158 --> 00:54:06,201
‪My name is

633
00:54:07,243 --> 00:54:08,703
‪Im Ho-won.

634
00:54:09,371 --> 00:54:10,372
‪My name is

635
00:54:11,706 --> 00:54:13,041
‪Kim…

636
00:54:14,250 --> 00:54:15,669
‪-Nice to meet you.
‪-Likewise.

637
00:54:16,294 --> 00:54:17,379
‪Please take care.

638
00:54:18,630 --> 00:54:19,714
‪-Take care.
‪-You too.

639
00:54:20,632 --> 00:54:21,466
‪Goodbye, then.

640
00:54:37,273 --> 00:54:39,609
‪ECOLOGICAL PARK

641
00:54:56,459 --> 00:54:57,794
‪-Min-ji.
‪-Yeah?

642
00:54:57,877 --> 00:54:59,170
‪Should we listen to some music?

643
00:55:05,260 --> 00:55:06,803
‪PLAYLIST FOR CHERRY BLOSSOM DAYS

644
00:55:25,864 --> 00:55:28,616
‪You know, people say you need new clothes
‪for a fresh start.

645
00:55:29,951 --> 00:55:32,078
‪Shouldn't I get
‪some new clothes too, then?

646
00:55:34,164 --> 00:55:36,207
‪Yeah, I should.

647
00:55:39,544 --> 00:55:40,712
‪I'm unemployed now.

648
00:55:42,547 --> 00:55:44,215
‪But you'll get a new job, right?

649
00:55:46,342 --> 00:55:47,177
‪Come on.

650
00:55:49,179 --> 00:55:50,263
‪All right.

651
00:55:50,346 --> 00:55:52,307
‪I'll buy you new clothes when I get a job.

652
00:55:52,891 --> 00:55:54,350
‪That's a promise, right?

653
00:55:54,434 --> 00:55:56,394
‪I'm going to ask for something
‪really expensive.

654
00:55:56,478 --> 00:55:57,395
‪All right.

655
00:56:22,712 --> 00:56:24,464
‪Your homeroom teacher is awful.

656
00:56:24,547 --> 00:56:27,884
‪How could he not even wish you good luck
‪when you're transferring?

657
00:56:27,967 --> 00:56:31,179
‪I heard things have been tense at school
‪because of Hye-ri.

658
00:56:31,262 --> 00:56:34,724
‪Yeah, I saw on social media that people
‪are calling it a school for criminals.

659
00:56:34,808 --> 00:56:36,101
‪I know.

660
00:56:49,697 --> 00:56:50,573
‪I guess

661
00:56:51,199 --> 00:56:52,951
‪you're really transferring.

662
00:56:54,035 --> 00:56:54,869
‪Yeah.

663
00:56:56,412 --> 00:56:57,413
‪I'm sorry.

664
00:56:58,164 --> 00:57:00,375
‪If only I hadn't messaged you that day…

665
00:57:04,295 --> 00:57:05,964
‪You didn't do it on purpose.

666
00:57:07,340 --> 00:57:08,174
‪It's okay.

667
00:57:10,301 --> 00:57:11,136
‪Then…

668
00:57:12,095 --> 00:57:13,179
‪Will you…

669
00:57:14,639 --> 00:57:16,182
‪message me after you transfer?

670
00:57:17,308 --> 00:57:18,268
‪I'll visit you.

671
00:57:22,439 --> 00:57:23,356
‪I don't think

672
00:57:24,524 --> 00:57:25,692
‪I can.

673
00:57:27,902 --> 00:57:28,778
‪Right.

674
00:57:29,571 --> 00:57:31,322
‪-I see.
‪-I'm sorry.

675
00:57:32,740 --> 00:57:34,451
‪No, don't be sorry.

676
00:57:40,748 --> 00:57:43,626
‪I think I should get going.

677
00:57:43,710 --> 00:57:44,711
‪Already?

678
00:57:44,794 --> 00:57:46,087
‪She's waiting for me.

679
00:57:48,548 --> 00:57:49,466
‪Take care.

680
00:58:05,815 --> 00:58:06,691
‪Here.

681
00:58:07,901 --> 00:58:11,613
‪KIM MIN-JI

682
00:58:11,696 --> 00:58:12,947
‪Will you…

683
00:58:14,073 --> 00:58:15,325
‪remember my name?

684
00:58:17,368 --> 00:58:18,203
‪Yeah.

685
00:58:19,078 --> 00:58:20,163
‪Kim Min-ji.

686
00:58:30,006 --> 00:58:31,007
‪How did it go?

687
00:58:33,885 --> 00:58:35,053
‪Let's go.

688
00:58:57,867 --> 00:58:58,910
‪This is it. What do you think?

689
00:58:58,993 --> 00:59:00,703
‪Oh my gosh, it's so pretty!

690
00:59:00,787 --> 00:59:02,163
‪-Come on, let's go.
‪-All right.

691
00:59:07,794 --> 00:59:09,337
‪Hey, Kim!

692
00:59:10,421 --> 00:59:12,257
‪Uncle?

693
00:59:13,883 --> 00:59:14,801
‪-Hey.
‪-Hey.

694
00:59:17,053 --> 00:59:18,680
‪Hey, what a great house.

695
00:59:19,430 --> 00:59:20,515
‪Is it a rental or did you buy it?

696
00:59:21,099 --> 00:59:23,142
‪Min-ji, did you do well on your exams?

697
00:59:23,226 --> 00:59:24,477
‪Of course.

698
00:59:24,561 --> 00:59:25,395
‪She's a level eight.

699
00:59:25,478 --> 00:59:26,813
‪Wow, level eight?

700
00:59:26,896 --> 00:59:28,523
‪-I'm jealous.
‪-What about Da-bin?

701
00:59:29,107 --> 00:59:31,025
‪-She's healthy.
‪-That's all that matters.

702
00:59:31,109 --> 00:59:31,943
‪Hey, Kim.

703
00:59:37,532 --> 00:59:39,867
‪Hey, why are there so many boxes?

704
00:59:39,951 --> 00:59:41,077
‪Do we have to move all of this?

705
00:59:41,160 --> 00:59:42,036
‪Oh my.

706
00:59:42,745 --> 00:59:43,913
‪Hey.

707
00:59:44,497 --> 00:59:46,249
‪So you <i>‪do</i>‪ own other clothes.

708
00:59:47,584 --> 00:59:48,626
‪You look great.

709
00:59:50,044 --> 00:59:52,255
‪I told you I have a lot of clothes.

710
00:59:53,256 --> 00:59:54,924
‪-You look really rich.
‪-Do I?

711
00:59:56,217 --> 00:59:58,177
‪Hey, hold on.

712
00:59:58,261 --> 00:59:59,846
‪We're moving boxes,
‪and you came dressed like that?

713
00:59:59,929 --> 01:00:00,847
‪Yeah.

714
01:00:00,930 --> 01:00:02,140
‪Why?

715
01:00:02,223 --> 01:00:04,642
‪Well, you know, it's a special day.

716
01:00:05,810 --> 01:00:06,894
‪Have you lost your mind?

717
01:00:06,978 --> 01:00:08,563
‪Be honest. You wore this
‪to avoid working, didn't you?

718
01:00:08,646 --> 01:00:10,857
‪I'm tired. Stop talking to me.

719
01:00:10,940 --> 01:00:11,858
‪You're tired?

720
01:00:11,941 --> 01:00:15,528
‪Eat one of these, get an energy boost,
‪and start moving boxes.

721
01:00:17,822 --> 01:00:21,618
‪And one for each of you
‪before you get to work.

722
01:00:22,785 --> 01:00:23,745
‪Here.

723
01:00:24,287 --> 01:00:25,413
‪And one for me too.

724
01:00:27,874 --> 01:00:29,626
‪This tastes just like coffee.

725
01:00:30,543 --> 01:00:31,377
‪It's good.

726
01:00:31,878 --> 01:00:34,505
‪Just how many of those
‪do you have at home?

727
01:00:34,589 --> 01:00:35,965
‪-Do you want a box?
‪-I sure do.

728
01:00:36,049 --> 01:00:37,258
‪Are you moving in or not?

729
01:00:37,342 --> 01:00:38,259
‪Coming!

730
01:00:38,343 --> 01:00:40,136
‪Hey, let's finish up quickly and go eat.

731
01:00:40,219 --> 01:00:42,555
‪-Hurry up and unload.
‪-Get a move on!

732
01:00:42,639 --> 01:00:43,848
‪-Here we go.
‪-Let's go.

733
01:00:43,931 --> 01:00:45,892
‪-Move some boxes, punk.
‪-Okay.

734
01:00:45,975 --> 01:00:47,268
‪-All right.
‪-Let's go.

735
01:00:47,352 --> 01:00:48,645
‪-Quickly, quickly.
‪-What are you doing?

736
01:00:48,728 --> 01:00:50,438
‪-Hurry up now.
‪-Hurry up!

737
01:00:50,521 --> 01:00:52,815
‪All right, here we go.

738
01:00:57,904 --> 01:00:59,781
‪-That's the last one, right?
‪-Yeah.

739
01:01:00,365 --> 01:01:01,783
‪Yeah, you little weasel.

740
01:01:01,866 --> 01:01:03,660
‪You didn't even lift a finger.

741
01:01:03,743 --> 01:01:05,495
‪All you did was carry the light boxes.

742
01:01:05,578 --> 01:01:07,664
‪How can you look Min-ji in the eye?

743
01:01:07,747 --> 01:01:10,083
‪Hey, Kim Min-ji-min… Ji-min.
‪Why are you laughing?

744
01:01:10,166 --> 01:01:13,711
‪Do you want to see me get hurt
‪while carrying heavy boxes?

745
01:01:13,795 --> 01:01:15,797
‪No, of course not.

746
01:01:16,547 --> 01:01:18,091
‪Let's go eat. I'll take care of the rest.

747
01:01:18,174 --> 01:01:20,176
‪Why bother? Let's just order <i>‪jjajangmyeon</i>‪.

748
01:01:20,760 --> 01:01:22,261
‪-<i>‪Jjajangmyeon</i>‪ is the best on moving days.
‪-Hey.

749
01:01:22,929 --> 01:01:24,430
‪Why do you get to choose the menu?

750
01:01:24,514 --> 01:01:26,182
‪Eat whatever Min-ji wants to have.

751
01:01:26,265 --> 01:01:27,725
‪What do you want, Min-ji? You decide.

752
01:01:28,309 --> 01:01:30,520
‪-<i>Jjajangmyeon</i> sounds good to--
‪-Did you say sushi? Okay.

753
01:01:30,603 --> 01:01:31,688
‪Sushi sounds great.

754
01:01:32,355 --> 01:01:34,190
‪Your daughter wants sushi.

755
01:01:37,026 --> 01:01:38,861
‪You must really like sushi.

756
01:01:40,780 --> 01:01:43,282
‪-Yeah, I love it.
‪-See?

757
01:01:43,366 --> 01:01:45,034
‪Let's go have sushi.

758
01:01:45,827 --> 01:01:46,994
‪-Get changed first.
‪-Let's go change.

759
01:01:47,078 --> 01:01:49,497
‪-Han-soo, you're really something else.
‪-Okay.

760
01:01:51,416 --> 01:01:53,710
‪You know, come to think of it,
‪you always wear the same outfit.

761
01:01:55,712 --> 01:01:56,587
‪What are you looking at?

762
01:01:59,674 --> 01:02:01,843
‪Darn it, I can't see without my glasses.

763
01:02:02,593 --> 01:02:04,554
‪Hey, I want to see.

764
01:02:04,637 --> 01:02:06,806
‪-Let me take a look.
‪-You can just look at that.

765
01:02:06,889 --> 01:02:07,724
‪Oh, it's all here.

766
01:02:07,807 --> 01:02:09,851
‪-Thank you.
‪-Gosh, there are so many items.

767
01:02:09,934 --> 01:02:13,020
‪My stomach will be full of fish
‪swimming around.

768
01:02:13,104 --> 01:02:15,982
‪Hey, Kim Min-ji-min.
‪You made a spectacular choice.

769
01:02:16,065 --> 01:02:17,400
‪Order whatever you want.

770
01:02:17,483 --> 01:02:19,485
‪-What are you having?
‪-I think I'll have--

771
01:02:19,569 --> 01:02:22,071
‪Can we get one flounder…
‪Actually, make it five. What else?

772
01:02:22,697 --> 01:02:23,906
‪Don't be shy.

773
01:02:24,657 --> 01:02:26,993
‪And can we get five plates
‪of yellowfin tuna belly?

774
01:02:27,660 --> 01:02:29,370
‪Here, have salmon. You like it, right?

775
01:02:30,580 --> 01:02:31,789
‪You like it too.

776
01:02:32,290 --> 01:02:34,041
‪One more salmon, please.

777
01:02:34,125 --> 01:02:36,127
‪Make it five, please.
‪Do you want some too?

778
01:02:36,210 --> 01:02:37,795
‪-Of course.
‪-Actually, make it ten.

779
01:02:44,427 --> 01:02:46,220
‪Why are you eating with your hands?

780
01:02:46,846 --> 01:02:48,014
‪That's how you eat sushi.

781
01:02:52,351 --> 01:02:53,895
‪There's no eel here, what a shame.

782
01:02:59,317 --> 01:03:00,443
‪Is it good?

783
01:03:00,526 --> 01:03:02,528
‪Yeah, it's dangerously good.

784
01:03:02,612 --> 01:03:04,405
‪He wasn't asking you, Uncle.

785
01:03:04,489 --> 01:03:05,323
‪Sorry.

786
01:03:05,948 --> 01:03:06,949
‪It's good.

787
01:03:07,033 --> 01:03:07,867
‪Eat up.

788
01:03:07,950 --> 01:03:08,868
‪-Okay.
‪-Okay.

789
01:03:09,994 --> 01:03:10,995
‪Eat up, you guys.

790
01:03:11,078 --> 01:03:11,913
‪Okay.

791
01:03:12,705 --> 01:03:15,708
‪-Sir, you forgot the monkfish liver.
‪-What else do you want?

792
01:03:18,544 --> 01:03:21,297
<i>‪A new neighborhood, a new school…</i>

793
01:03:24,926 --> 01:03:27,261
<i>‪and a new name I don't like.</i>

794
01:03:31,724 --> 01:03:33,643
‪Min-ji, come have breakfast!

795
01:03:34,811 --> 01:03:35,895
‪Kim Min-ji!

796
01:03:37,688 --> 01:03:38,731
‪I'm late.

797
01:03:38,815 --> 01:03:40,817
<i>‪A lot of things have changed,</i>

798
01:03:40,900 --> 01:03:43,486
<i>‪but my dad and I haven't </i><i>‪changed</i>
<i>‪all </i><i>‪that </i><i>‪much.</i>

799
01:03:47,949 --> 01:03:50,409
‪I'll eat after I get back. Save me some.

800
01:03:52,203 --> 01:03:53,204
‪Okay, I will.

801
01:03:53,830 --> 01:03:54,872
‪Be safe.

802
01:03:55,873 --> 01:03:57,124
‪And don't get into any fights!

803
01:03:57,750 --> 01:03:59,168
‪I won't!

804
01:03:59,252 --> 01:04:02,004
<i>‪Except for my dad laughing more often now.</i>

805
01:04:03,005 --> 01:04:04,090
‪Hello, ma'am.

806
01:04:04,173 --> 01:04:06,092
‪Pure hearts, pure manners.
‪Join Pure Taekwondo.

807
01:04:06,175 --> 01:04:09,804
<i>‪-And my uncles are still the same.</i>
‪-We're offering free trial classes.

808
01:04:09,887 --> 01:04:10,721
‪Thank you.

809
01:04:10,805 --> 01:04:11,889
‪Hello.

810
01:04:11,973 --> 01:04:14,976
‪-Look who's back.
‪-We're offering free trial classes.

811
01:04:15,059 --> 01:04:16,894
‪-Who's that man over there?
‪-It's not on the flyer,

812
01:04:16,978 --> 01:04:20,356
‪but we play dodgeball,
‪and there are prizes, so come by, okay?

813
01:04:20,439 --> 01:04:21,524
‪-Hello, ma'am.
‪-Cross slowly!

814
01:04:21,607 --> 01:04:23,234
‪Please cross the street now.

815
01:04:23,317 --> 01:04:25,403
‪Pure Taekwondo
‪is located on the third floor.

816
01:04:25,486 --> 01:04:27,655
‪Feel free to drop by
‪during the free trial period.

817
01:04:27,738 --> 01:04:29,448
‪Hello, ma'am.

818
01:04:30,032 --> 01:04:31,284
‪Should we stop him?

819
01:04:31,868 --> 01:04:33,870
‪Leave him be. It's a nice sight.

820
01:04:33,953 --> 01:04:35,121
‪I bet he was a big club-goer.

821
01:04:35,204 --> 01:04:38,499
‪POLICE

822
01:04:42,587 --> 01:04:44,755
‪The weather is so nice.

823
01:04:45,506 --> 01:04:46,966
‪I know, right?

824
01:04:47,049 --> 01:04:48,759
‪It was really cold not too long ago.

825
01:04:48,843 --> 01:04:50,678
‪-Please enjoy.
‪-Thank you.

826
01:04:51,345 --> 01:04:52,346
‪Let's eat.

827
01:04:52,430 --> 01:04:53,472
‪This looks good.

828
01:04:53,556 --> 01:04:54,932
‪Hold on. We need to take a photo.

829
01:04:56,183 --> 01:04:58,644
<i>‪Sang-a hangs out with me sometimes.</i>

830
01:05:04,692 --> 01:05:05,568
‪Sang-a.

831
01:05:07,194 --> 01:05:09,155
‪You're here to keep an eye on me, right?

832
01:05:09,238 --> 01:05:10,865
‪No, I'm not.

833
01:05:10,948 --> 01:05:12,658
‪You think you're special?

834
01:05:12,742 --> 01:05:13,993
‪No.

835
01:05:14,076 --> 01:05:15,328
‪Who saved your life?

836
01:05:15,411 --> 01:05:16,245
‪You did.

837
01:05:16,329 --> 01:05:17,705
‪Then who should you be thanking?

838
01:05:17,788 --> 01:05:18,748
‪You?

839
01:05:18,831 --> 01:05:19,707
‪So who should pay for this?

840
01:05:20,875 --> 01:05:22,043
‪You?

841
01:05:24,378 --> 01:05:25,755
‪Right, I should pay.

842
01:05:25,838 --> 01:05:26,756
‪Dig in.

843
01:05:26,839 --> 01:05:28,716
‪Thank you.

844
01:05:30,217 --> 01:05:32,011
‪How are things with your dad?

845
01:05:32,094 --> 01:05:33,429
‪Is he more affectionate than before?

846
01:05:35,139 --> 01:05:37,308
‪No, he's still the same.

847
01:05:37,391 --> 01:05:38,225
‪Right.

848
01:05:38,309 --> 01:05:40,436
‪That's not really who he is, is it?

849
01:05:40,519 --> 01:05:41,812
‪It's totally not him.

850
01:05:42,313 --> 01:05:44,106
‪Any good news lately, Sang-a?

851
01:05:45,024 --> 01:05:49,028
‪-He was like, "You can't date yet."
‪-Really?

852
01:05:49,946 --> 01:05:51,155
‪I'm not surprised.

853
01:05:58,788 --> 01:06:00,915
‪Allow me to present today's special.

854
01:06:03,417 --> 01:06:05,586
‪These would be good for when I do this.

855
01:06:09,131 --> 01:06:11,217
‪Do you have regular glasses
‪instead of sunglasses?

856
01:06:12,677 --> 01:06:13,594
‪Who are you?

857
01:06:15,846 --> 01:06:17,723
‪I usually don't show this to anyone,
‪but here goes.

858
01:06:18,307 --> 01:06:20,101
‪"Brother Monkey, what's gotten into you?"

859
01:06:20,977 --> 01:06:22,561
‪Hello.

860
01:06:22,645 --> 01:06:24,438
‪My name is Kim. Nice to meet you.

861
01:06:26,774 --> 01:06:29,443
‪In my opinion, this case is…

862
01:06:30,444 --> 01:06:31,946
‪Rock and roll.

863
01:06:38,369 --> 01:06:39,537
‪Hey, Han-soo, Jin-cheol.

864
01:06:40,121 --> 01:06:41,288
‪You think Min-ji will approve?

865
01:06:42,581 --> 01:06:43,582
‪Probably not.

866
01:06:43,666 --> 01:06:46,544
‪Hey, what do you think?
‪They suit me, right?

867
01:06:46,627 --> 01:06:47,545
‪-You look weird.
‪-You look weird.

868
01:06:47,628 --> 01:06:48,504
‪Damn it.

869
01:06:49,005 --> 01:06:51,048
‪Just kidding.
‪You look like Tony Leung Chiu-wai.

870
01:06:51,132 --> 01:06:54,051
‪Tony Leung Chiu-wai, my foot.
‪He looks like a brewery owner.

871
01:06:54,135 --> 01:06:57,555
‪Hey, you look like a middle-aged man
‪desperate to look young.

872
01:06:57,638 --> 01:06:58,723
‪That's what we are.

873
01:06:59,974 --> 01:07:00,975
‪Right.

874
01:07:01,851 --> 01:07:02,768
‪We're middle-aged men.

875
01:07:03,352 --> 01:07:04,437
‪Middle-aged men with glasses.

876
01:07:06,605 --> 01:07:09,150
‪Now that I'm wearing glasses again
‪after a while,

877
01:07:09,775 --> 01:07:11,569
‪I feel like
‪they're weighing my shoulders down.

878
01:07:11,652 --> 01:07:12,778
‪Should we take them off?

879
01:07:12,862 --> 01:07:16,157
‪No. It's better to be
‪middle-aged men with glasses.

880
01:07:17,283 --> 01:07:18,200
‪-Let's go.
‪-Okay.

881
01:07:19,076 --> 01:07:20,828
‪-Goodbye, sir.
‪-Oh, goodbye.

882
01:07:20,911 --> 01:07:21,829
‪-Thank you.
‪-Goodbye.

883
01:07:21,912 --> 01:07:23,581
‪-Have a good day.
‪-Take care.

884
01:07:23,664 --> 01:07:26,667
‪-There wasn't much to choose from.
‪-You tried on 145 pairs.

885
01:07:33,758 --> 01:07:36,469
‪It feels pretty good
‪to wear new glasses though.

886
01:07:36,552 --> 01:07:38,929
‪Yeah, I feel like I could fly!

887
01:07:40,014 --> 01:07:41,098
‪Hey, mister.

888
01:07:41,891 --> 01:07:44,393
‪You should never mess with
‪middle-aged men with glasses.

889
01:07:44,477 --> 01:07:46,896
‪-Yeah, someone could get someone hurt.
‪-Who?

890
01:07:46,979 --> 01:07:49,607
‪The one who messed with them
‪or the middle-aged men with glasses?

891
01:07:50,232 --> 01:07:51,108
‪I'm not sure.

892
01:07:52,485 --> 01:07:55,613
<i>‪All dads in the world</i>
<i>‪are just regular people.</i>

893
01:07:56,197 --> 01:07:57,948
<i>‪-They work to support their families,</i>
‪-What's with the color?

894
01:07:58,032 --> 01:07:59,909
<i>‪-and they're afraid of moms.</i>
‪-Guys, check it out.

895
01:07:59,992 --> 01:08:01,744
<i>‪-And sometimes after work</i>‪…
‪-Did you ask for these?

896
01:08:01,827 --> 01:08:03,037
‪They're transition lenses.

897
01:08:03,120 --> 01:08:05,039
‪-…<i>‪they come home with smelly feet.</i>
‪-I didn't ask for these though.

898
01:08:05,122 --> 01:08:06,207
‪They give off a middle-aged man vibe.

899
01:08:06,290 --> 01:08:07,291
‪Man, these are slick.

900
01:08:07,374 --> 01:08:11,796
<i>‪It may be hard to believe, but my dad</i>
<i>‪is also just a regular middle-aged man.</i>

901
01:08:14,840 --> 01:08:15,674
<i>‪Well,</i>

902
01:08:16,300 --> 01:08:18,219
<i>‪as long as no one messes with me.</i>

903
01:08:22,264 --> 01:08:27,895
‪HAPPINESS ROAD, HAENGBOK-RO

904
01:08:38,114 --> 01:08:43,035
‪BAEKHO LABOR AGENCY

905
01:08:45,871 --> 01:08:46,789
<i>‪Oh, I almost forgot.</i>

906
01:08:47,373 --> 01:08:49,166
<i>‪I think my dad's getting a new job.</i>

907
01:08:50,709 --> 01:08:53,420
<i>‪Someone he knew back in the day</i>
<i>‪introduced him to it.</i>

908
01:08:59,969 --> 01:09:01,846
<i>‪Juhak Construction is nothing.</i>

909
01:09:01,929 --> 01:09:05,099
<i>‪I'll chop it up like a cucumber</i>

910
01:09:05,182 --> 01:09:07,560
<i>‪and make a salad out of it.</i>

911
01:09:08,144 --> 01:09:10,104
<i>‪You know this will cost you, right?</i>

912
01:09:13,482 --> 01:09:14,817
‪3RD FLOOR

913
01:09:34,587 --> 01:09:35,629
‪May I help you?

914
01:09:41,260 --> 01:09:42,094
‪Excuse me.

915
01:09:42,887 --> 01:09:44,180
‪I'm here for an interview--

916
01:09:44,263 --> 01:09:45,514
‪Check and check!

917
01:09:45,598 --> 01:09:48,309
‪I just checked your résumé, Kim!

918
01:09:49,185 --> 01:09:50,769
‪But you know,

919
01:09:51,353 --> 01:09:55,691
‪I'm not sure if I can trust this.

920
01:09:59,028 --> 01:10:00,279
‪Now then.

921
01:10:00,362 --> 01:10:02,156
‪Shall we start

922
01:10:02,239 --> 01:10:03,782
‪the interview?

923
01:10:47,368 --> 01:10:50,287
‪AGENT KIM REACTIVATED

924
01:10:54,375 --> 01:11:00,297
‪STAY TUNED FOR A BONUS SCENE

925
01:11:30,661 --> 01:11:34,373
‪AGENT KIM REACTIVATED

926
01:11:34,456 --> 01:11:36,041
‪BONUS SCENE

927
01:11:36,125 --> 01:11:40,087
‪IN 2006, THERE WAS A FAMOUS TRIO
‪IN THE CHEONSAN UNIT

928
01:11:43,632 --> 01:11:44,591
‪CHEONSAN

929
01:12:00,357 --> 01:12:01,942
‪Korea's iron teeth!

930
01:12:02,735 --> 01:12:04,194
‪They're unbreakable!

931
01:12:05,946 --> 01:12:07,531
‪Korea's iron teeth!

932
01:12:39,396 --> 01:12:42,441
‪PARK JIN-CHEOL

933
01:12:42,524 --> 01:12:44,318
‪YOON KYUNG-HO

934
01:12:44,401 --> 01:12:47,363
‪SUNG HAN-SOO

935
01:12:47,446 --> 01:12:49,323
‪CHOI DAE-HOON

936
01:12:49,406 --> 01:12:52,534
‪KIM

937
01:12:52,618 --> 01:12:57,539
‪SO JI-SUB

938
01:12:57,623 --> 01:12:59,249
‪AGENT KIM REACTIVATED

939
01:12:59,333 --> 01:13:01,668
‪Subtitle translation by:
